Runners in GitHub Actions

Today I explored runners, the machines that actually execute CI/CD jobs in GitHub Actions.

🔹 GitHub-Hosted Runners
Managed by GitHub
Preconfigured environments
Auto-scaled and maintained
Best for quick CI/CD setups

🔹 Self-Hosted Runners
Managed by users
Run on own infrastructure
More control & customization
Useful for private networks

🔹 Runner Selection
Workflows can specify:
OS type
Runner labels
Custom environments
Correct selection ensures compatibility.

🔹 Security Considerations
Limit runner access
Isolate sensitive jobs
Protect secrets
Monitor runner usage

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Runners execute workflows.
 Choice affects security.
 Control impacts performance.
